<title>FRANCE: Suez, Lyonnaise to cut St Gobain stake.</title>
<headline>Suez, Lyonnaise to cut St Gobain stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The merged group Suez Lyonnaise des Eaux plans to cut its stake in glass group Saint-Gobain, in line with its strategy of untangling cross shareholdings, Suez chairman Gerard Mestrallet said.</p>
<p>Lyonnaise des Eaux and Cie de Suez on Friday said they planned to merge.</p>
<p>Jerome Monod, head of Lyonnaise and chairman designate of the supervisory board of the merged group, told an analysts meeting that Belgian businessman Albert Frere, who controls Groupe Bruxelles Lambert, aimed to bring his stake in the merged group to the 8.3 percent he currently has in Suez.</p>
</text>
